hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19569","Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from al-Shabi, from Urwah al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks, and reward and spoils, until the Day of Resurrection."
"19570","Sufyan informed us, al-Bariqi Shabib informed us that he heard Urwah al-Bariqi say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied to their forelocks. And I saw in his house seventy horses."
"19571","Sufyan narrated to us, from Shabib, that he heard the clan informing from Urwah al-Bariqi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with him a dinar to buy for him a sacrifice - and once he said: or a sheep - and he bought two for him, sold one for a dinar, and brought him the other. He supplicated for him for blessing in his trade. He would, if he bought dust, profit in it."
"19572","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Zakariyya, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad."
"19573","Abu Kamil narrated to us, from Said ibn Zayd, from al-Zubayr, from Abu Labid, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad."
"19574","And Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad - all of them: Ibn Abi al-Jad said."
"19575","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
"19576","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Zakariyya, and Waki said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from Amir, from Urwah - Yahya said: Ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Waki said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
"19577","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar, from Urwah ibn Jad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks."
"19578","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
"19579","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, Abu Labid narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi, he said: A caravan met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave me a dinar and said: O Urwah, go to the caravan and buy for us a sheep. I went to the caravan, bargained with its owner, and bought from him two sheep for a dinar. I came driving them, or he said: leading them, and a man met me and bargained with me, and I sold him a sheep for a dinar. I came with the dinar and I came with the sheep, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your dinar and this is your sheep. He said: And what did you do. He said: I told him the story, and he said: O Allah, bless him in the deal of his right hand. I saw myself standing at the rubbish-heap of Kufah, gaining forty thousand before reaching my family. And he used to buy slave-girls and sell."
"19580","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Abu Labid, and he is Lumazah ibn Zabbar, from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"19581","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: I heard al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth narrating from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Azdi that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied to their forelocks."
"19582","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Husayn and Abdillah ibn Abi al-Safar informed me that they heard al-Shabi hear Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
"19583","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Shabi, Urwah al-Bariqi narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
"19584","Affan narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit narrated to us, from Abu Labid, he said: Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi was staying among us, and Abu Labid Lumazah ibn Zabbar narrated from Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad, he said: A caravan met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave me a dinar and said: O Urwah, go to the caravan and buy for us a sheep. He said: I went to the caravan, bargained with its owner, and bought from him two sheep for a dinar. I came driving them, or he said: leading them, and a man met me and bargained with me, and I sold him a sheep for a dinar. I came with the dinar and I came with the sheep, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your dinar and this is your sheep. He said: And what did you do. I told him the story, and he said: O Allah, bless him in the deal of his right hand. I saw myself standing at the rubbish-heap of Kufah, gaining forty thousand before reaching my family. And he used to buy slave-girls and sell."
"19585","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, he said: I heard Urwah ibn Abi al-Jad al-Bariqi, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Horses have good tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection: reward and spoils."
